        },
        {
          "case": "endpoints",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "No endpoint case occurs in the claim."
        },
        {
          "case": "nonempty-choice",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Proof3.1 constructs every allocation coordinate by the single explicit expression nstar N_h S_h/sum_k N_k S_k. The denominator is positive and finite under the hypotheses, and2.1 proves uniqueness, so the optimizer is a formula rather than an arbitrary choice from a set of minimizers."
        },
        {
          "case": "iff-forward",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Proof2.1: attaining the global lower bound forces every pair square(p_h q_k-p_k q_h)^2 to vanish, so a_h/x_h is constant. The positive size constraint normalizes it uniquely to x_h=nstar a_h/sum a_k as in3.1."
        },
        {
          "case": "iff-reverse",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Proof3.1 explicitly constructs x_h=nstar a_h/sum a_k, verifies positivity and the size constraint, and makes each pair square in2.1 vanish. It therefore attains the global lower bound and is the unique minimum."
